0 Worm Drive
0 Name: worm-drive.ldr
0 Author: erik-larsen
0 // A worm on a crossways axle driving a 24 tooth gear below it: 24 turns of the worm turn the
0 // gear once. A worm can't be driven from its gear (it locks), so turning the gear does nothing.
0 // The worm's axle is 40 LDU (2 studs) above the gear's, the worm's and gear's pitch radii added.

0 // Step 1: a 6x8 plate, with a 1x6 brick and a Technic 1x6 brick on top along each side
1 72 0 0 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3036.dat
1 14 0 -24 50 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3009.dat
1 14 0 -24 -50 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3009.dat
1 14 0 -48 50 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3894.dat
1 14 0 -48 -50 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3894.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 2: the gear's axle through the middle holes, with the 24 tooth gear in the middle
1 0 0 -38 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3707.dat
1 71 0 -38 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3648.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 3: Technic plates bridging the bricks at each end, each with a 1x2 plate and a
0 // Technic 1x2 brick on top, turned so their holes run along x, 40 LDU above the gear's axle
1 71 60 -56 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3738.dat
1 71 -60 -56 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3738.dat
1 14 50 -64 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3023.dat
1 14 -50 -64 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3023.dat
1 14 50 -88 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3700.dat
1 14 -50 -88 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 3700.dat
0 STEP

0 // Step 4: the worm's axle along x through the Technic bricks, with the worm over the gear
1 0 0 -78 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 3707.dat
1 72 0 -78 0 0 0 1 0 1 0 -1 0 0 4716.dat
0 STEP
